  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 126 AM EDT Thu May 14 2026\n\nHigh pressure over the area continues into the extended periods \nkeeping things mostly dry through the beginning of next week. For \nnow it looks like our biggest concern will be the increased day time \nhigh temps as we go into the weekend and next week. By Sat morning a \nweek wave moves SE out of the Central Plains and into KY/TN. We will \nsee some increase moisture across the state but still not expecting \nany precip. Mainly increased cloud cover but temps will get up into \nthe 80s to near 90. These elevated temps continue through day 7 with \na slight chance of precip expected by Tue as the ridge begins to \nbreak down. For now only going with a 20% chance of showers and \nisolated thunderstorms as not exactly to confident on how fast the \nridge will break down.  \n\nFire weather may end up being a concern into the weekend with RH \nvalues potentially in the 25-30% range but thankfully winds should \nremain relatively light. Please continue to monitor the Fire Weather \nForecast for potential critical fire weather.",
